<h2>Transaction events</h2>
<p>Transaction events record activity on a loan account, such as disbursal, payout refund, adding or waiving a fee, adding or reversing a repayment, goodwill credit, goodwill reversal, charge-off, discount fee amortization, chargeback, balance write-off, debt sale, and account closure.</p>
<p>Each transaction event maps to a business event:</p>
<ul>
<li>Repayment triggers WorkingCapitalLoanRepaymentTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Goodwill credit triggers WorkingCapitalLoanGoodWillCreditTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Payout refund triggers WorkingCapitalLoanPayoutRefundTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Discount fee triggers WorkingCapitalLoanDiscountFeeTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Discount fee adjustment triggers WorkingCapitalLoanDiscountFeeAdjustmentTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Discount fee amortization triggers WorkingCapitalLoanDiscountFeeAmortizationTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Discount fee amortization adjustment triggers WorkingCapitalLoanDiscountFeeAmortizationAdjustmentTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Charge adjustment triggers WorkingCapitalLoanChargeAdjustmentBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Credit balance refund triggers WorkingCapitalLoanCreditBalanceRefundTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Disbursement triggers WorkingCapitalLoanDisbursalTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Charge-off triggers WorkingCapitalLoanChargeOffTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Accrual triggers WorkingCapitalLoanAccrualTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Accrual adjustment triggers WorkingCapitalLoanAccrualAdjustmentTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Write-off triggers WorkingCapitalLoanWriteOffTransactionBusinessEvent.</li>
<li>Adding a charge triggers WorkingCapitalLoanAddChargeBusinessEvent.</li>
</ul>
